# Direct self-spawns are routed back through the conformance runner. These
# remaining files require a process-host facility the current environment does
# not expose, or mix an ordinary typed contract with a Section 13 assertion.
test-process-exit-code.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); the final case dynamically removes process._fatalException to observe Node bootstrap status 6, while local/exit-code-static.js retains the ten ordinary exit and uncaught-exception cases
test-process-exit-code-validation.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); deletes process.exitCode to inspect descriptor non-configurability, while local/exit-code-validation-static.js retains all value normalization and exit cases
test-process-kill-pid.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); its valid-case table dynamically replaces process._kill, while local/kill-validation.js retains argument validation and test-process-kill-null.js retains real signal delivery
test-process-raw-debug.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); dynamically replaces process.nextTick and stderr.write, while local/raw-debug-format.js retains formatting and direct native-sink behavior
test-process-really-exit.js: language non-goal (§13); its sole assertion dynamically replaces the undocumented process.reallyExit method
test-process-emitwarning.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); replaces Error.toString on individual instances, while local/emitwarning-static.js retains all statically representable overload, event, detail, and validation cases
test-process-warning.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); replaces stderr.write and Error.toString at runtime, while local/warning-policy.js retains non-Error suppression, deprecation suppression/throw, default type, and detail behavior
test-process-remove-all-signal-listeners.js: active-environment gap; needs signal watchers so the first SIGINT emits on the typed process and removing its last listener restores default OS termination
test-process-external-stdio-close.js: active-environment gap; the routed fork needs child IPC message delivery and process.disconnect on the substituted process
test-process-external-stdio-close-spawn.js: active-environment gap; the routed IPC spawn needs child IPC message delivery and process.disconnect on the substituted process
test-process-getgroups.js: treats an absent getgroups as success even on POSIX, so empty-module sabotage is hollow; the same `id -G` oracle runs without that optional guard in local/getgroups.js
test-process-redirect-warnings.js: active-environment gap; the routed child needs startup-option normalization and a warning-file sink for --redirect-warnings
test-process-redirect-warnings-env.js: active-environment gap; the routed child needs startup environment policy and a warning-file sink for NODE_REDIRECT_WARNINGS
test-process-warnings.mjs: runtime blocker; the process host does not yet expose its normalized --no-warnings/--no-deprecation/repeated --disable-warning/NODE_OPTIONS snapshot, while local/warning-policy.js retains direct warning emission and writable policy behavior

# The API itself is implemented in its final WeakRef/FinalizationRegistry form,
# and local/finalization.js retains every process-local upstream fixture. The
# remaining upstream cases require an independent runtime registry inside a
# Worker, which a single-environment addon must refuse rather than share.
test-process-finalization.mjs: cross-module integration; Worker-local process.finalization needs one isolated runtime per Node Environment, while local/finalization.js retains exit, beforeExit, GC cleanup, unregister, and argument validation

# A dynamically selected builtin has no object type or static link target. The
# final implementation depends on the planned runtime module registry plus a
# generic object-handle representation; neither exists in the current ABI.
test-process-get-builtin.mjs: runtime blocker; getBuiltinModule needs the planned runtime builtin-module registry and heterogeneous object handles rather than the current link-time module graph

# Successful `execve` replaces the inner runner. The outer local observer can
# still grade the replacement's status, arguments, environment, lifecycle, and
# descriptor inheritance; local/execve-success.js retains those public cases.
# The unchanged fixtures cannot be used because they exec their vendored `.js`
# path, which the checkout's root `type: module` then reinterprets as ESM.
# `test-process-execve-validation.js` stays directly applicable because every
# call throws before reaching the replacement boundary. The no-argument test
# remains enrolled and reports Node's own environment skip when its `nop`
# fixture binary is unavailable.
test-process-execve.js: harness/package boundary; after replacing the inner runner, the root `type: module` reinterprets this CommonJS `.js` fixture as ESM; local/execve-success.js retains argv, environment, and successful replacement
test-process-execve-on-exit.js: harness/package boundary; after replacing the inner runner, the root `type: module` reinterprets this CommonJS `.js` fixture as ESM; local/execve-success.js retains the no-exit-event contract
test-process-execve-socket.js: harness/package boundary; after replacing the inner runner, the root `type: module` reinterprets this CommonJS `.js` fixture as ESM; local/execve-success.js retains close-on-exec socket behavior
test-process-execve-permission-fail.js: needs --permission to deny the call
test-process-execve-permission-granted.js: needs --permission to allow the call
test-process-execve-worker-threads.js: needs worker_threads to be the caller

# NTS has no runtime property map or intrinsic graph (§13). These tests are
# specifically about V8 exotic objects, property descriptors/prototypes, or
# Node's private binding/addon loader, so their behavior cannot be represented
# by the profile's flat statically typed objects.
test-process-abort.js: checks observable function prototype/constructor metadata, a §13 non-goal
test-process-binding.js: process.binding/internalBinding expose Node's private intrinsic native-module graph
test-process-binding-internalbinding-allowlist.js: process.binding exposes Node's private intrinsic native-module graph
test-process-binding-util.js: process.binding exposes Node's private intrinsic native-module graph
test-process-config.js: asserts recursive Object.freeze behavior and writable property descriptors
test-process-constants-noatime.js: tests node:fs.constants only and never observes process
test-process-dlopen-error-message-crash.js: process.dlopen loads Node-ABI native addons through Node's private module loader
test-process-dlopen-undefined-exports.js: process.dlopen loads Node-ABI native addons through Node's private module loader
test-process-domain-segfault.js: V8 regression test only assigns legacy process.domain and has no observable process assertion
test-process-prototype.js: inspects the process prototype chain and constructor property descriptor
test-process-ref-unref.js: language non-goal (§13); the public API accepts any and dynamically dispatches Symbol.for('nodejs.ref'/'nodejs.unref') hooks with string-named fallbacks

# `process.env` is a V8 interceptor: arbitrary property get/set/delete/define
# operations call getenv/setenv and even change the engine timezone. NTS has no
# exotic objects or Proxy (§13). The supported subset is a readonly snapshot;
# direct snapshot/loadEnvFile coverage is kept in local/env-snapshot-load.js.
test-process-env-delete.js: requires live exotic property writes and deletes
test-process-env-deprecation.js: requires the exotic setter and its coercion warning
test-process-env-ignore-getter-setter.js: tests Object.defineProperty descriptors on the exotic env object
test-process-env-sideeffects.js: asks V8 Inspector to evaluate an exotic env property interceptor
test-process-env-symbols.js: tests Symbol-key traps on the exotic env object
test-process-env-tz.js: requires the exotic setter to call the JavaScript engine's timezone hook
test-process-env-windows-error-reset.js: requires live exotic get/set/has interception even on the POSIX lane
test-process-env.js: requires live exotic get/set/delete/has behavior and propagates it to a spawned host Node
test-process-load-env-file.js: four cases spawn host Node and the remaining direct cases are isolated in local/env-snapshot-load.js

# These upstream files mix a supported static subset with a §13 operation.
# Focused local files preserve the supported assertions without claiming the
# excluded metaobject behavior.
test-process-env-allowed-flags.js: mixes flag membership/iteration with Object.freeze and direct Set.prototype mutation; see local/allowed-flags.js
test-process-env-allowed-flags-are-documented.js: validates Node's generated CLI documentation, which is absent from the pinned source-only checkout; runtime membership is covered by local/allowed-flags.js
test-process-hrtime.js: mixes public timing behavior with eval/V8 optimization intrinsics and internalBinding; see local/time-and-versions.js
test-process-hrtime-bigint.js: mixes supported `hrtime.bigint` behavior with eval/V8 optimization intrinsics and internalBinding; see local/time-and-versions.js
test-process-versions.js: asserts property descriptors for every version entry, a §13 non-goal; see local/time-and-versions.js

# Dynamic import is a wanted compiler feature, not a permanent language
# non-goal. This fixture remains inapplicable to the current CommonJS
# conformance lane for the independent harness reason below: its ESM loader
# resolves Node's builtin directly and never receives the substituted module.
test-process-default.js: harness limitation; dynamically imports host node:process rather than the substituted module, while dynamic import itself remains required compiler work

# These calls deliberately terminate the conformance child before it can
# report a verdict. Focused parent/child fixtures preserve the exact terminating
# behavior rather than replacing the native exit operation.
test-process-exit-from-before-exit.js: runner limitation; process.exit terminates the runner from a beforeExit listener, covered by local/exit-from-before-exit.js
test-process-exit-recursive.js: runner limitation; recursive process.exit terminates the runner from an exit listener, covered by local/exit-recursion.js

# JavaScript source-map cache toggling belongs to Node/V8's code-generation
# engine. NTS emits native debug information and has no eval/generated-JS source
# map subsystem to toggle.
test-process-setsourcemapsenabled.js: requires Node's V8 source-map cache subsystem

# Workers execute this upstream file in fresh host Node isolates, outside the
# CommonJS substitution. The main-thread CPU accounting behavior has its own
# applicable upstream test.
test-process-threadCpuUsage-worker-threads.js: worker copies use host node:process, not the module under test

# These public process tests live outside the test-process-* naming family.
# The applicable nextTick/resource tests are enumerated in extra-tests. These
# three cannot provide a non-hollow verdict against the supported static API.
test-memory-usage.js: requires V8-specific external/ArrayBuffer heap accounting; the supported NTS allocation record is isolated in local/resource-accounting.js, while `memoryUsage.rss` is covered by the applicable EMFILE fixture
test-next-tick-domain.js: only proves that loading host node:domain does not replace a function; an absent nextTick passes unchanged under sabotage
test-next-tick-when-exiting.js: runner limitation; process.exit terminates before the verdict, while local/next-tick-when-exiting.js retains the typed _exiting transition and nextTick suppression during exit
